.SH NAME
ktm-vec \- Growable arrays and bit vectors.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
import vec;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Growable arrays and bit vectors.
.SH TYPES
.SS BitVec
.EX
struct BitVec {
    i64 blocks;
    u32 *entries;
};
.EE
.SS Vec
.EX
struct Vec<T> {
    T *data;
    i64 len;
    i64 cap;
};
.EE
.PP
A growable array of T, held by value (like String): make one with vec.new<T>(), free it with free() (or declare it \fBscoped\fR). A Vec of String owns its Strings: free() and clear() free them, and set() frees the one it replaces; pop() and removeAt() hand the item back to you. Other items are yours: free() frees the array, not what pointers in it point to. An index outside 0..len-1 throws ERR_BOUNDS, as a slice index does.
